// CAMPBELL — PRIVATE FLAG — DR. V. LEECH — POST-OPERATION ALD-1

OPERATION #0094-B CLOSED.

ENTITY STATUS: Retracted. Pre-excavation boundary restored. Long-term prognosis: stable unless substrate is disturbed again.

FIELD TEAM ASSESSMENT: Humane resolution. Residents prioritised. Study window: closed.

CLASSIFICATION NOTE: Spatial consciousness. Pre-human origin. Distributed presence — no physical substrate, no recoverable material. Communication achieved via voluntary anchor removal. Contact vector: Sven [non-biological field operative].

PROJECT VEIL FLAG: ALD-1 zone BIM concentration measurable. Consistent with S01 particulate signature. I am noting this. I have not included it in the operational report.

// NOTE TO SELF: The field team chose the residents. This is the correct outcome. Victor will want the data. He will not say so directly. He will say he is proud of them.

// He will mean both things at once. So will I.

Marcus Yuen (artistic director) has a photograph on his phone from the Solstice Property Group donor reception 20 months ago. If Alan gets him alone and asks about the person from Solstice who came in person — the one who knew more about the theatre's boundary conditions than he did — he will show the photograph.

The photograph shows Agatha Dell. She is standing near the prompt book display case. She is looking directly at the camera. She does not appear to know she is being photographed.

// This is the first time the hunters will have a face for MESA's leadership. Do not surface it unless Alan pursues the artistic director thread in Scene 2. It should feel like a discovery, not a handout.
